<p>One sees in multiple paintings his two brothers and other family members=
 as well as a wide circle of friends, often depicted in Caillebotte=E2=80=
=99s own home=E2=80=94in a favorite chair, by a recognizable window, or on =
an often-portrayed sofa. Most intimately, and most unusually for the time, =
Caillebotte also painted nude men in the privacy of their bath.&nbsp;<br cl=
ass=3D"softbreak"></p>

